    "title": "Kaya's Busy Day",
    "sentences": [
      "Kaya woke up quite sleepy; it was a rainy morning.",
      "Her fourth period moral education was followed by quick arts and crafts in the studio.",
      "She made a thin paper design and practiced calligraphy.",
      "At 2 p.m., Kaya went to brass band practice, not far.",
      "She thought about an important date: the day after tomorrow.",
      "It was a swimming pool party for her age group.",
      "Kaya needed to research lemonade; home economics taught seasoning like soy sauce.",
      "She would use about one ounce of sugar.",
      "She wanted a free minute to think, “Don’t worry.”",
      "Kaya pictured an amusement park, a scream, hoping to catch fun.",
      "Such thoughts made her smile; she took a photograph.",
      "She would take off her wet playground shoes."
    ]
